<Layout locale="en" title="About Astrmira · A research-driven company" description="Astrmira is a research-driven company exploring foundational questions and building open systems across data and intelligence." route="about">
  <div class="wrap"><section class="page-title"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / ASTRMIRA</p><h1>Grounded in research.<br /><em>Open to wonder.</em></h1><p>Astrmira—幻梦星芒 in Chinese—is a research-driven company. We work across databases, retrieval, vectors, quantization, post-training, and mathematics, while exploring paths from research ideas to usable systems.</p></section>
    <section class="directory-content"><div class="value-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">FIRST PRINCIPLES</p><h3>Ask what is fundamental.</h3><p>Begin with explicit questions, assumptions, and constraints. We want to understand why a method works and where its boundary lies.</p></div><div><p class="eyebrow">IDEAS INTO SYSTEMS</p><h3>Let ideas meet reality.</h3><p>Theory and engineering inform one another. Research enters real systems, and real problems open new research questions.</p></div><div><p class="eyebrow">SHARED DISCOVERY</p><h3>Explore with peers.</h3><p>Research and university partnerships connect different experience around questions worth sustained attention.</p></div></div></section>
  </div>
  <section class="wrap origin-section" data-star-anchor="origin"><OriginArtwork /><div class="origin-copy"><p class="eyebrow">A NOTE ON OUR NAME</p><h2>A wonderful star.<br /><em>A lasting curiosity.</em></h2><p class="origin-cn">Stars change. Curiosity continues.</p><p>Astr evokes the distant sky; Mira is a real variable star; Mirage is an imagined horizon still to be reached. We call this image 幻梦星芒—a wonderful star.</p><p style="margin-top:13px">Mira changes in brightness and leaves a long ultraviolet tail. For us, it describes a research attitude: keep imagination alive around the unknown, and leave a trail that others can continue.</p><a class="source-link" href="https://science.nasa.gov/universe/exoplanets/the-tail-of-a-wonderful-star/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Name inspiration · NASA / The Tail of a Wonderful Star ↗</a></div></section>
</Layout>
